SUMMARY:John Clyde Native Grassland Preserve Birds and Butterflies
DESCRIPTION:Led by Chris and Paula Williams\, Associate Naturalists \nJoin the Williams for a walk through the fields and forest of this grassland preserve to look for butterflies\, resident NJ birds\, late migrant birds passing through\, and anything else nature will be showing. Grasshopper Sparrow\, Bobolink\, and American Kestrel\, state threatened species\, are found on this site. Bring binoculars if you have them.  This site is one of the first grassland restoration projects NJ Audubon has implemented for Franklin Township Open Space Committee. This program is funded by the Franklin Township Open Space Committee. \n\nCOST: FREE\n\n\n\n\nLOCATION: 1091 Canal Road\, Princeton\, NJ   \nREGISTRATION: Please register with Franklin Township by email: Tara.Kenyon@franklinnj.gov  \n 
URL:https://njaudubon.org/event/john-clyde-native-grassland-preserve-birds-and-butterflies/
LOCATION:John Clyde Memorial Native Grasslands Preserve\, 1091 Canal Rd\, Princeton\, NJ\, United States
CATEGORIES:Bird Walk,Birding,Nature Walk,Scherman Hoffman Wildlife Sanctuary
GEO:40.4323244;-74.6125243
