UID:10010896-1779352200-1779366600@njaudubon.org
SUMMARY:Warren Park/Oros Preserve
DESCRIPTION:Spring songbird migrants at two productive urban oases. Good days can produce a dozen or more species of warblers\, plus thrushes & vireos. These Middlesex County hotspots provide green oases for migratory species. Warren Park (at the border of Woodbridge & Perth Amboy) has an excellent hardwood forest—complete with understory that is excellent for thrushes\, vireos\, and warblers; we’ll also visit the Oros Wildlife Preserve where pin oaks\, brushy fields\, and a large pond/wetland will complement the day’s bird list. Oros Preserve is sometimes muddy\, so hiking shoes or other footwear you don’t mind getting a little dirty are best. A spotting scope is not necessary for this trip. Led by Scott Barnes and Patrick Belardo. PRE-REGISTRATION REQUIRED \nA NOTE ON MEETING LOCATION! Some navigational devices may take you to a condo complex adjacent to the park. Take a moment to make sure you go to the right location. Once you enter the park\, you will come to a T intersection. Turn left and follow this road clockwise until it ends in a wooded parking lot north of what the park map calls “The Open Grove.” \nCOST: $25 Members\, $30 Non-members \nWEATHER & TRANSPORTATION: Please arrive at the appointed time. Be sure to check the forecast in advance and dress in layers appropriate for prevailing weather conditions. We sometimes bird in the rain\, so bring rain gear if warranted. Transportation during the field trip is by private vehicle (be sure you have enough gas). Most trips involve some amount of walking\, sometimes through muddy or sandy terrain. \nCANCELLATION: NJA/CMBO programs require a minimum number of registrants to run\, five days in advance of the start of the tour but are seldom cancelled. If we do cancel\, due to lack of participation\, severe weather\, or unforeseen circumstances\, we notify all participants in advance\, and all are eligible for a full credit or refund. Participants may cancel without penalty if greater than 30 days in advance. Cancellations 10 to 30 days in advance may be subject to a 25% service charge. No refunds or credits for cancellations less than ten days in advance unless due to health emergencies. \nREGISTER HERE
URL:https://njaudubon.org/event/warren-park-oros-preserve-16/
LOCATION:William Warren Park\, Florida Grove Road\, Woodbridge Township\, NJ\, 07095\, United States
CATEGORIES:All Things Birds,Bird Walk,Birding
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://njaudubon.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/11/Warren-Park-Oros-Preserve-spring-2025.jpg
GEO:40.5411852902;-74.2829487467
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=William Warren Park Florida Grove Road Woodbridge Township NJ 07095 United States;X-APPLE-RADIUS=500;X-TITLE=Florida Grove Road:geo:-74.2829487467,40.5411852902
END:VEVENT
